skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: the decision to stop choosing an agent's model by environment, and everything that stops having a home when it lands
' would touch: defs/bridges/** (the four tables, deleted outright)
' would touch: internal/provider/slots.go (BridgeTable, ResolvedEnv), internal/provider/roles.go (RoleVars, Roles)
' would touch: internal/entrypoint/** (the alias bridges), packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh (apply_model_bridges)
' would touch: defs/{cecli,claudecode/mcp,cursor,opencode}/entrypoint.sh
' would touch: internal/run/{run,spec,params,choices}.go, internal/backend/sandbox/sandbox.go (ResolvedModelEnv)
' would touch: cmd/proveo/main.go, cmd/proveo-entrypoint/main.go, embed.go
' would touch: _spec/internal/provider/{model-catalog,model-resolution}.puml, _spec/internal/entrypoint/model-alias-bridges.puml
' APPLIED 2026-09-09, except Q2. The questions below were put to the operator
' before any deletion; their answers are recorded under each one. The plan is
' kept in _plans/ rather than moved, because Q2 is still open and this is where
' the reader looking for it will come.
'
' ── SECOND PASS, SAME DAY: THE DELETION LANDED, THE LOOP DID NOT CLOSE ─────
' Asked to assert this plan complete, and it was not. The src half was done and
' `go test ./...` was green, but the VERIFICATION half — persisted tests, e2e,
' the docs a contributor reads — still described the mechanism, and two of the
' plan's own recorded answers were FALSE IN PRACTICE. All of it is closed now,
' and what follows is what was wrong, because each item is a way for a deletion
' to look finished while it is not.
'
' 1. Q1's ANSWER WAS FALSE FOR OPENCODE. Its seeds wrote
'    ""model"": ""{env:OPENCODE_MODEL}"" into every slot, and the bridge tables
'    were what filled that variable. opencode substitutes an UNSET ""{env:...}""
'    with the EMPTY STRING (opencode.ai/docs/config), so from the deletion
'    onward the seed pinned the model to nothing — and pinned it in the DURABLE
'    HOME, where it outlives the run. "The agent's own default applies" was the
'    recorded answer; what actually applied was "". FIXED: the seeds name no
'    model at all, and ""plan""/""build"" omit their own so a primary agent
'    inherits the global (opencode.ai/docs/agents). The file with a real default
'    baked in, ""defaults/opencode.json"", is NOT the one seeded — see the open
'    item at the bottom.
'
' 2. Q2 WAS NOT ACTUALLY PRESERVED. "Nothing on the PROVEO_LOCAL_MODEL path was
'    touched" is true of that path's own code and false of its effect, because
'    opencode is THE ONE HARNESS whose local model was named only by the bridge.
'    cecli's entrypoint writes CECLI_MODEL from PROVEO_LOCAL_MODEL itself and
'    claudecode gets ANTHROPIC_MODEL from ""docker -e"" (internal/egress/plan.go);
'    opencode's ""configure_opencode_local_model"" REGISTERED the ollama provider
'    and left ""apply_model_bridges"" to select it. So ""--local-model opencode""
'    wired a provider nothing chose. FIXED: that block now also sets ""model"" and
'    ""small_model"" and exports the two OPENCODE_* vars the PROVEO_MODELS
'    preamble reports. e2e/hello_world_test.go's ""assertModels"" would have caught
'    this — eight minutes into a docker run, on a lane that needs a live Ollama.
'
' 3. TWO DEF IMAGE SUITES STILL ASSERTED THE BRIDGE, and this is the structural
'    lesson: they need a BUILT IMAGE, so they are invisible to ""go test ./...""
'    and the deletion looked green.
'      defs/cursor/tests/test_config.sh   3 tests — ARCHITECT_MODEL becomes
'                                         CURSOR_MODEL, an explicit CURSOR_MODEL
'                                         outranks it, EDITOR_MODEL fills in
'      defs/opencode/tests/test_config.sh 2 tests — role names become the three
'                                         OPENCODE_* vars, and the reverse bridge
'    All five now assert the RETIREMENT: that a role name reaches the harness as
'    nothing, and that the harness's OWN var still does. One of them was passing
'    by accident either way — it grepped ""SMALL_MODEL=xai/grok-4.3"" and
'    ""OPENCODE_SMALL_MODEL"" matched it as a SUBSTRING.
'
' 4. THE DOCS STILL ASKED FOR IT. CODING_HARNESSES.md instructed entrypoints to
'    bridge the three names and to normalise bare ids — a standing instruction to
'    re-add exactly what was deleted, in the file a new harness is written from.
'    .claude/skills/sync-models cited ""PlanFallback"" and
'    ""TestPlanFallbacksAreRealModels"", both deleted here, so its verification step
'    named a test that does not exist. Both rewritten; the skill now says outright
'    that its catalog has no reader pending Q4.
'
' 5. _spec/.spec-index.json pointed at internal/contract/model_slots_test.go,
'    deleted in the same commit that left the pointer.
'
' 6. FIVE SPEC FILES still described the mechanism as live — opencode's and
'    cecli's paradigms, the hello-world e2e's three assertions, egress-tiers'
'    broker pin (roles resolve it from a REMEMBERED assignment now, not the
'    environment), and cecli's ""covers: defs/bridges/cecli.tsv"".
'
' WHAT NOW GUARDS IT (internal/contract/model_bridging_retired_test.go):
'   no seed names a model by environment · --local-model still selects one for
'   opencode · all three harnesses name their local model without a role name ·
'   the harness doc does not ask for role bridging · the def suites assert the
'   retirement rather than the bridge.
'   The three pre-existing shell guards were comment-BLIND and fired on the
'   prose explaining the deletion. They read code now, because this repo's habit
'   is to name the deleted machinery exactly where it used to live, and a guard
'   that forbids the explanation is a guard someone deletes.
'
' STILL OPEN, DELIBERATELY: Q2 and Q4 as written below; ""localModelArgs""
' (internal/egress/plan.go) still writes the three role names on the docker
' local-model path, inert; and opencode ships TWO default configs that disagree —
' ""sample_opencode.json"" is what ""seed_opencode_config"" copies and now names no
' model, while ""defaults/opencode.json"" still hard-codes
' ""anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-5"" and is read only for AGENTS.md. Whether a seeded
' id is proveo choosing (forbidden here) or the agent's own saved config (the
' DECISION's own replacement mechanism) is config-seeding's question, not this
' one's.
'
' ── WHAT WAS DECIDED, AND WHAT LANDED ──────────────────────────────────────
'   Q1  ANSWERED: the agent's own default. proveo sets no model env at all.
'   Q2  DEFERRED: "we will revisit for e2e, full local model support". Nothing
'       on the PROVEO_LOCAL_MODEL path was touched.
'   Q3  ANSWERED: Roles survive as the CREDENTIAL vocabulary.
'   Q4  NOT ASKED, and therefore NOT DONE. The catalog and sync-models are
'       untouched; with nothing resolving an id they have no reader today.
'   Q5, Q6  fell out of Q1: there is no first-run announcement, and the
'       `apply_model_bridges` call sites are removed rather than emptied.
'
' WHAT LANDED
'   deleted  defs/bridges/ (4 tables + README) · internal/provider/slots.go
'            (BridgeTable, LoadBridges, ResolvedEnv, EffectiveSlots,
'            RefusedSlots, Refusal, applyTransform) · embed.ModelBridges ·
'            run.Deps/Spec.ModelBridges · Params.Bridges · sandbox.Input.Bridges
'            and ResolvedModelEnv · posture.MergeRoles · the four
'            `COPY defs/bridges/` layers · apply_model_bridges and
'            _apply_model_bridge and their four call sites
'   pruned   roles.go lost RolesFrom (the env read), Canonical, canonicalModel,
'            ResolveRoles, PlanFallback and the planFallback table
'   renamed  RoleVars -> RoleNames. The three names survive as the KEYS of a
'            remembered assignment; nothing reads them from the environment,
'            and a name saying "Vars" would invite exactly that back
'   rewritten posture.RolesLine renders roles directly — there is no slot table
'            left to ask which variable a role becomes
'
' ── TWO THINGS THE APPLICATION LEARNED, BOTH WORTH KEEPING ─────────────────
' 1. THE CREDENTIAL BRIDGES ARE A DIFFERENT MECHANISM WITH THE SAME NAME, and
'    deleting the model half took them with it on the first attempt.
'    `_apply_env_bridge` / `apply_env_bridges` map GEMINI_API_KEY onto
'    GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY — a CREDENTIAL, not a model — and
'    `internal/entrypoint`'s Go/bash parity test caught the loss immediately.
'    `entrypoint.ApplyEnvBridges` likewise stays: it never bridged a model.
'
' 2. `localModelArgs` (internal/egress/plan.go:387) STILL WRITES the three role
'    names on the docker local-model path, and nothing reads them any more. They
'    are INERT rather than wrong, and they were left alone because Q2 is
'    deferred — but they are the first thing to look at when it is answered.
'
' The DECISION at the top is the operator's and is not re-argued. Everything
' below it is either MEASURED or a QUESTION.
'
'   where a saved config lives .... _spec/_plans/config-seeding-and-persistence.puml
'   what resolves an id today ..... _spec/internal/provider/model-resolution.puml
'   the catalog behind it ......... _spec/internal/provider/model-catalog.puml
'   the bridge tables ............. _spec/internal/entrypoint/model-alias-bridges.puml
'   where roles are also DISPLAYED  _spec/internal/choiceui/wireframe.puml
'   and where they gate billing ... _spec/internal/credentials/credential-decisions.puml
'   the prior art for a deletion .. _spec/_plans/retire-docker-egress.puml
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── THE DECISION, STATED ONCE AND NOT ARGUED FOR ───────────────────────────
' Retire the bridging of model choice by environment, completely. Strip
' ARCHITECT_MODEL, EDITOR_MODEL and SMALL_MODEL from proveo and remove the
' bridging to every agent. An agent's model comes from ITS OWN SAVED CONFIG,
' carried between sessions by the durable home. That is the operator's decision.
' This plan records it, measures what it costs, and asks what has nowhere to go.
'
' ── WHAT IS TRUE TODAY — MEASURED ──────────────────────────────────────────
' 1. THE SURFACE IS 45 FILES FOR THE THREE NAMES ALONE, plus 17 more carrying
'    bridge machinery: internal/provider/roles.go (311 lines), slots.go (228),
'    internal/entrypoint/entrypoint.go (283), the four defs/bridges/*.tsv
'    tables (10 lines in total), four def entrypoints, internal/run/**,
'    internal/backend/sandbox (ResolvedModelEnv), both cmd/** binaries and
'    embed.go. Roughly fourteen spec files describe some part of it.
'
' 2. THE TABLES DO FOUR JOBS, NOT ONE, and only the first is "pick a model".
'    Read defs/bridges/opencode.tsv:
'        main   OPENCODE_MODEL  ARCHITECT_MODEL,EDITOR_MODEL
'                               anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-5  normalize  -
'    columns: role, the agent's OWN vars, proveo's role vars, a DEFAULT, a
'    normalisation mode, a provider pin. So a table also supplies a default
'    where the operator chose nothing, normalises an id into the shape that
'    harness accepts, and pins a provider (claudecode.tsv pins `anthropic`).
'    Deleting the role-var column is not the same as deleting the file, and the
'    plan should not assume the other three columns have no readers.
'
' 3. THE ROLE VARS ARE ALSO READ WHERE NO MODEL IS BEING SET.
'    `provider.RoleVars` (roles.go:11) feeds the credential and billing surface
'    — `Roles.MissingKeys` warns which keys a chosen set of models needs, and
'    the choice UI's wireframe draws roles as rows. Those readers do not write
'    an agent's environment and do not obviously die with the bridging.
'
' 4. THERE IS NO USER-FACING `--model` FLAG TO ORPHAN. The only model-ish flag
'    on cmd/proveo is `--local-model` (LocalModel). So this retirement does not
'    leave a dead CLI switch behind — which is the failure retire-docker-egress
'    catalogued for the egress tier, and it does not repeat here.
'
' 5. THE SUBSTRATE FOR "SAVED CONFIG" ALREADY EXISTS AND IS ALREADY SPECIFIED.
'    `home.enabled` mounts each agent's own config into the durable home —
'    .cecli.conf.yml, .claude.json, opencode.json, cli-config.json — and
'    config-seeding-and-persistence.puml owns that chain. The decision leans on
'    machinery that is PARTLY LANDED there (its steps 3-5 are not implemented),
'    so the two plans are now coupled and each should say so.
'
' 6. THE BRIDGING IS ALSO HOW A BAD ID BECAME A WARNING. MEASURED from a cecli
'    run: proveo wrote `CECLI_MODEL=claude-opus-5`, cecli split it on "/",
'    found no provider, and printed "Unknown which environment variables are
'    required" three times. That is an argument FOR the decision, not against:
'    the bridge was shaping an id for a consumer whose rules it did not model.
'
' ── THE OPEN QUESTIONS. NONE OF THESE IS ANSWERED HERE ─────────────────────
' Q1. WHAT HAPPENS ON A FIRST RUN, where no saved config exists yet? The agent
'     falls to its own built-in default — aider's for cecli, and for opencode
'     that means LOSING the `anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-5` default the table
'     supplies today. Is the agent's own default the intended answer, or does
'     proveo SEED the config file once and never touch it again? The second is
'     config-seeding's shape, not bridging's, and it is a different change.
'
' Q2. WHAT BECOMES OF `PROVEO_LOCAL_MODEL`? Ollama rides the SAME path:
'     apply_model_bridges plus OPENAI_API_BASE / ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL written by
'     each def's entrypoint. Retiring bridging removes local-model support
'     unless it is carved out — and a carve-out means the mechanism survives
'     for one caller, which is a smaller deletion than the one decided.
'
' Q3. DO ROLES SURVIVE AS A CONCEPT? main/editor/weak name a shape the
'     credential UI and the billing verdict both use (MEASURED 3). Is this
'     "remove the env-writing and keep Roles as a credential vocabulary", or
'     "delete roles.go and slots.go outright" — 539 lines, and with them the
'     only machine-readable statement of which key each role needs?
'
' Q4. WHAT HAPPENS TO THE CATALOG AND ITS SKILL? model-resolution.puml and
'     model-catalog.puml exist to turn an operator's shorthand into an id a
'     harness accepts, and .claude/skills/sync-models keeps them current. With
'     nothing resolving an id, do they retire too, or survive as VALIDATION —
'     warning that a saved config names a model that no longer exists? The
'     second keeps a reader for the catalog; the first deletes a fact nobody
'     else writes down.
'
' Q5. WHERE DOES THE OPERATOR CHOOSE, AFTERWARDS? Today the answer is "proveo,
'     before the run". After this it is "inside the agent, once, and it sticks".
'     That is a real UX change and it should be stated rather than discovered:
'     does proveo say so on a first run, or does the operator meet an agent on
'     an unexpected model and go looking for a setting proveo no longer has?
'
' Q6. WHAT DOES A DEF'S ENTRYPOINT STILL DO? `apply_model_bridges <target>` is
'     called by all four. Does the call site go, or does it become the seam
'     that reads a saved config? A no-op left in place is how a later reader
'     concludes the mechanism still exists.
title APPLIED + VERIFIED (Q2, Q4 open) — retire model bridging: what chooses a model once the environment stops

component "**the decision**\nno model choice by environment" as DECISION <<error>>

node "what is bridged today" as BRIDGE <<host>> {
  component "defs/bridges/*.tsv\nrole · agent vars · role vars\ndefault · normalise · pin" as TSV <<app>>
  component "provider.RoleVars\nARCHITECT · EDITOR · SMALL" as ROLES <<app>>
  component "BridgeTable.ResolvedEnv\nslots.go:202" as RESOLVE <<app>>
  component "apply_model_bridges\ncalled by all four entrypoints" as APPLY <<app>>
}

database "the agent's own saved config\n.cecli.conf.yml · .claude.json\nopencode.json · cli-config.json" as SAVED <<db>>
component "config-seeding-and-persistence\nsteps 3-5 NOT landed" as SEED <<error>>

component "the credential + billing surface\nRoles.MissingKeys · choiceui rows" as CREDS <<app>>
component "the model catalog\n+ .claude/skills/sync-models" as CAT <<app>>
component "PROVEO_LOCAL_MODEL\nollama, same code path" as LOCAL <<error>>
component "opencode's DEFAULT\nanthropic/claude-sonnet-4-5" as DEFAULT <<error>>

DECISION ARROW_ERROR BRIDGE : deleted
TSV ARROW_MAIN RESOLVE
ROLES ARROW_MAIN RESOLVE
RESOLVE ARROW_MAIN APPLY
DECISION ARROW_MAIN SAVED : the replacement
SAVED ARROW_QUEUE SEED : leans on a plan that is PARTLY landed
ROLES ARROW_MAIN CREDS : Q3 — a reader that sets no model
TSV ARROW_MAIN DEFAULT : Q1 — nothing supplies this afterwards
APPLY ARROW_MAIN LOCAL : Q2 — the same path, a different caller
RESOLVE ARROW_MAIN CAT : Q4 — the catalog's only consumer

note bottom of TSV
  **MEASURED. A table does FOUR jobs.**
  Role vars are one column of six. Default,
  normalisation and provider pin are the others,
  and deleting the column is not the same as
  deleting the file.
end note

note right of ROLES
  **MEASURED. Roles are read where no model
  is set.** ""Roles.MissingKeys"" warns which key
  a set of models needs and the choice UI draws
  them as rows. Neither writes an agent's
  environment.
end note

note bottom of DEFAULT
  **Q1 — who supplies a first run?**
  opencode's table names sonnet-4-5 and
  haiku-4-5 today. With the table gone the
  agent's own default applies, and for a fresh
  machine that is the whole answer.
end note

note bottom of LOCAL
  **Q2 — does ollama go too?**
  It rides ""apply_model_bridges"" and the
  base-URL writes in each entrypoint. A
  carve-out keeps the mechanism alive for one
  caller, which is a smaller deletion.
end note

note bottom of CAT
  **Q4 — retire, or become validation?**
  With nothing resolving an id the catalog has
  no reader. As a VALIDATOR it warns that a
  saved config names a model that is gone —
  which keeps a fact nobody else writes down.
end note

note top of SAVED
  **MEASURED. The substrate exists.**
  ""home.enabled"" already mounts each agent's
  config into the durable home. What is not
  landed is steps 3-5 of config-seeding, so
  these two plans are now coupled.
end note

note bottom of SEED
  **Q1's other half.** Seeding a config file
  ONCE is config-seeding's shape, not
  bridging's. If that is the answer, this
  deletion waits on that plan rather than
  replacing it.
end note

note top of DECISION
  **What the decision buys, in one measured case.**
  proveo wrote ""CECLI_MODEL=claude-opus-5"";
  cecli split it on "/", found no provider, and
  warned three times. The bridge was shaping an
  id for rules it did not model.
end note

legend bottom
  **What this plan is, and is not**
  ==
  **IS** — one decision recorded verbatim, six measured facts about what the bridging
  actually does, and six questions with no answers written into them.
  --
  **IS NOT** — a sequence of steps. The surface is ~60 files and the order depends on Q1
  and Q2; committing to an order now would smuggle in answers this file does not have.
  ==
  **The two that gate everything else**: Q1 (what a first run gets) and Q2 (whether
  local-model survives). Both decide whether this is a DELETION or a MOVE, and a move
  wearing a deletion's name is the outcome to avoid.
  --
  **Both of those answers were wrong in practice on the first pass**, and in the same
  place: opencode was the one harness whose model — first-run default AND local model —
  was named ONLY by the bridge. Every other harness names its own. See the second-pass
  block at the top of this file.
  --
  **The coupling to declare**: config-seeding-and-persistence.puml owns the durable home
  this decision leans on, and its steps 3-5 are not implemented. That plan should
  cross-reference this one in both directions before either moves.
end legend
@enduml
